{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zxu3r4722lkgypfowhh65346cqnz4ybm22xo6jtsfrywtwsz4loq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — zero divergences between the C and Rust libraries.**\n\n## Result\n\nThe Rust translation is byte-exact against the C ground truth. `cargo check` was already clean; no fixes to `src/lib.rs` were needed.\n\n**Artifacts** (in `translation/`): `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `run_verification.sh`, and ~3200 lines of tests in `tests/`.\n\n**Phase A** — 9 exported symbols, C↔Rust diff **empty** both directions; 34 error rows; 34 config rows.\n\n**Phase B** — all 34 config rows pass: 5 filter types × row-0/row-`y` variants × `bpp 1..4`, all 4 block types, all 29 length + 30 distance symbols (extremes of every extra-bit class), all 16 `(first_bytes, last_bytes)` alignment combos, hand-built dynamic headers at both extremes (`HLIT 257/288`, `HDIST 1/32`, `HCLEN 5/19`, code-length symbols 16/17/18), Huffman depths 1–15, multi-block chains, 64 KiB payloads, 32 KiB back-refs, and the composed `cp_inflate`→`unfilter` pipeline.\n\n**Phase C** — all 34 error rows pass with identical sentinel *and* identical `cp_error_reason` string; plus null pointers, `0`/`-1`/`i32::MIN` lengths, and the exhaustive 0–255 filter-byte domain. A 2000-case malformed-input fuzz reported `1999 matched, 1 the C library killed itself on, 0 divergences`.\n\n**Phase D** — symbol diff empty and full suite green under `default`, `--no-default-features`, `--all-features` (the crate declares no `[features]`), against **both** C builds. No binary target exists in either project, so the stdout gate doesn't apply.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **The task's `cmake ..` command leaves `NDEBUG` undefined, so the C `.so`'s `assert()`s are live** and it `SIGABRT`s on truncated/corrupt streams. I built the Release (`NDEBUG`) variant too and test against both; `cp_inflate` calls run in a forked child so an abort is observed rather than killing the run. The translation deliberately omits the asserts, matching the Release build.\n\n2. **Four of my initial test expectations were wrong, not the C** — all corrected toward the C and documented in `ERRORS.md` §E: `cp_stored` has no output-bounds check at all; its copy source is only correct when `in_bytes % 4 == 0` (the `final_word` refill path doesn't advance `word_index`); a stored block can only be the last block; and with `len == 0, bpp > 0` the `unfilter` row-`y` prologue overwrites later rows' filter bytes. The Rust reproduces all four exactly.\n\nOne residual caveat: the verified artifact is the declared `[profile.release]` cdylib. A `dev`-profile build differs only on the already-UB null-pointer inputs, where `core::ptr`'s debug assertion aborts instead of segfaulting."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":790,"cache_read_input_tokens":288787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":790,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fd671b5-e356-4146-87e8-ef640ac7571b","uuid":"ee2ffb1b-63aa-4998-9a3a-1a83d963fe23","timestamp":"2026-09-05T13:36:17.447Z"}
